  "dietSummary": "Mostly fed by the algae living in its mantle, which turn light into food. It also filters some phytoplankton from the water; small clams need more of it.",
  "temperamentSummary": "Sits fixed to the rock or sand with its bright mantle spread in the light. Peaceful: it snaps shut with a squirt of water when a shadow or a hand passes over it.",
  "careNotes": [
    "Needs strong light: about 250-400 PAR. Place it high on the rock or on the sand right under the lights.",
    "Bleaches (loses its colour and its food) in too little light, too much heat, or a sudden jump in light.",
    "Uses calcium and alkalinity for its shell like a stony coral; keep them steady.",
    "Some angelfish, crabs and big shrimp pick at the mantle. Watch for tiny white pyramidal snails on the shell at night.",
    "Do not pull it off the rock: the byssal threads under the hinge tear."
